{"path": "/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/13005/comments", "params": {"per_page": 100}, "body": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/4160461890", "html_url": "https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/13005#issuecomment-4160461890", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/13005", "id": 4160461890, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBWBCuM73-5xC", "user": {"login": "Viicos", "id": 65306057, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjY1MzA2MDU3", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65306057?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos", "html_url": "https://github.com/Viicos", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-03-31T07:16:25Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-31T07:16:25Z", "body": "Please look for duplicates, and also you shouldn't worry about `pydantic-core`as a dependency at all. `pydantic` hard pins `pydantic-core`, so having `pydantic-core`as an explicit dependency on your end isn't the right thing to do.", "author_association": "MEMBER", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/4160461890/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/4160512416", "html_url": "https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/13005#issuecomment-4160512416", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/13005", "id": 4160512416, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBWBCuM73_GGg", "user": {"login": "Tromador", "id": 38956076, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTU2MDc2", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38956076?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador", "html_url": "https://github.com/Tromador", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-03-31T07:27:04Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-31T07:27:04Z", "body": "Duplicate fair, I didn't look in closed issues.\n\nBut pydantic wants core as a dependency. When I tested this a couple of days ago, it pulled the latest core. Have you changed pydantic to hard pin it back to the older core? If not then the dependancy chain has the same result. ", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/4160512416/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/4160535997", "html_url": "https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/13005#issuecomment-4160535997", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/13005", "id": 4160535997, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBWBCuM73_L29", "user": {"login": "Viicos", "id": 65306057, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjY1MzA2MDU3", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65306057?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos", "html_url": "https://github.com/Viicos", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-03-31T07:32:03Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-31T07:32:03Z", "body": "Pydantic defines a `==`dependency on pydantic-core, as seen here:\n\nhttps://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/blob/ee8a3131a4676504040664d9bb39e2fb3e8fe8ae/pyproject.toml#L46-L50\n\nSo if you run `pip install pydantic`, it should pull the corresponding `pydantic-core` version. However, depending on how you install pydantic, this might not be respected.", "author_association": "MEMBER", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/4160535997/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/4160586228", "html_url": "https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/13005#issuecomment-4160586228", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/13005", "id": 4160586228, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBWBCuM73_YH0", "user": {"login": "Tromador", "id": 38956076, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTU2MDc2", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38956076?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador", "html_url": "https://github.com/Tromador", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tromador/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-03-31T07:42:17Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-31T07:42:17Z", "body": "It's being pulled in from something else. Pywebview, I think, but I'd need to check. I guess my workaround is ugly, but it does fix my problem for now. Thank you for the advice. ", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/4160586228/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}]}